So, we need some additional checks here. i.e. we need to make sure that if people free the event source from the callback we don't fuck up. i.e. i think something like this:

```c
if (s->ratelimit_expire_callback) {
                s->dispatching = true;
                r = s->ratelimit_expire_callback(s, s->userdata);
                s->dispatching = false;

                if (r < 0) {
                        log_debug_errno(r, "Ratelimit expiry callback of event source %s (type %s) returned error, %s: %m",
                                        strna(s->description),
                                        event_source_type_to_string(s->type),
                                        s->exit_on_failure ? "exiting" : "disabling");

                        if (s->exit_on_failure)
                                (void) sd_event_exit(e, r);
                }

                if (s->n_ref == 0)
                        source_free(s);
                else if (r < 0)
                        sd_event_source_set_enabled(s, SD_EVENT_OFF);
```
(Setting `s->dispatching` ensures that the event source is not actually freed even if the last reference is dropped by the callback. We then need to catch up with the ref count below)
